# ble-mcp

MCP server and CLI for BLE-controllers LED strips family **ELK-BLEDDM / ELK-BLEDOM / ELK-BTC / LEDBLE / MELK**. Written in TypeScript, works via BlueZ (D-Bus), **no native builds**.

The same logic is available in two ways:

- **MCP** — tools for agents (opencode, Claude Desktop, any MCP client). Transports: `stdio` and **streamable HTTP**.
- **CLI** — operations manually from terminal, outside the agent environment.

## Requirements

- **Linux** with BlueZ (tested on 5.85). Does not work on macOS/Windows (BLE devices cannot be addressed by MAC on macOS; node-ble requires BlueZ on Linux).
- **Node.js >= 20**
- Bluetooth adapter enabled (`bluetoothd` running)

No extra privileges required (BlueZ allows regular users to access `org.bluez` by default).

## Installation

```sh
cd ~/dev/apps/ble-mcp
npm install
npm run build
```

## Quick Start

```sh
ble-mcp scan
ble-mcp config --set-address BE:27:CB:00:46:7A --set-name ELK-BLEDDM
ble-mcp on
ble-mcp white 60
```

The launcher `~/.local/bin/ble-mcp` is already installed and points to `dist/index.js`.

